<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Graphics on STEP Batch 12</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/tags/graphics/</link><description>Recent content in Graphics on STEP Batch 12</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en_US</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:31:04 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://step-12.github.io/tags/graphics/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Simple exercises</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/first_exercises/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/first_exercises/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="first-exercises"&gt;First Exercises&lt;a class="anchor" href="#first-exercises"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You now have a working Raylib program.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You have seen how a Raylib program is structured, and you have used functions such as &lt;code&gt;r.DrawRectangle&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Now it is time to start solving some small problems.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For these exercises, create a directory called:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;workspace/raylib_exercises/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each exercise should be its own program.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Use these filenames:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;01_center_rectangle.js&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;02_center_rectangle_in_rectangle.js&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;03_scale_and_center.js&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;04_closer_target.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Write the Raylib program yourself for each exercise. You should not need to copy the program from the previous post.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raylib anatomy</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/anatomy/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/anatomy/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="the-anatomy-of-a-raylib-program"&gt;The anatomy of a Raylib program&lt;a class="anchor" href="#the-anatomy-of-a-raylib-program"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In the previous post, we saw that Raylib is a library that gives our JavaScript programs a collection of functions for working with graphics.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We are now going to look at a complete Raylib program.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Don&amp;rsquo;t worry if you don&amp;rsquo;t understand everything in it yet.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In fact, you shouldn&amp;rsquo;t.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Read through it once and see if you can recognize anything.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;require&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;raylib&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;InitWindow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Raylib&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SetTargetFPS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WindowShouldClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BeginDrawing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ClearBackground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BLACK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;DrawRectangle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WHITE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;EndDrawing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;CloseWindow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are quite a few things happening here.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Intro to Graphics/Raylib</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/intro/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/intro/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="raylib"&gt;Raylib&lt;a class="anchor" href="#raylib"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, most of the programs you have written have produced things like numbers and text.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You might have written:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;and seen:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Or perhaps you wrote a function that takes some values, performs a computation, and returns another value.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;What if the result of our program could be something that we could &lt;strong&gt;see&lt;/strong&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;What if instead of producing:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;our program could produce a rectangle on the screen?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That is where we are going next.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>